  "final_answer": "Google Flights kept returning \"Oops, something went wrong\" for Chicago to London on 20–23 Dec 2026, so I ran the search on Kayak. Prices are round-trip for 1 adult in economy, as Kayak showed them. I only read the first part of the results, so there are more options further down the page.\n\n**Nonstop options (ORD to LHR)**\n- **Iberia, $1,767:** Out on 20 Dec at 6:40 pm, arriving 8:35 am+1 (7h 55m). Back on 23 Dec at 11:00 am, arriving 1:45 pm (8h 45m).\n- **Iberia, $1,767:** Same outbound at 6:40 pm. Back on 23 Dec at 12:35 pm, arriving 3:35 pm (9h 00m).\n- **Iberia, $1,767:** Out at 8:05 pm, arriving 10:00 am+1 (7h 55m). Back at 11:00 am, arriving 1:45 pm.\n- **Iberia, $1,767:** Out at 8:05 pm, arriving 10:00 am+1. Back at 12:35 pm, arriving 3:35 pm.\n- **British Airways, $1,778:** Out at 6:40 pm, arriving 8:35 am+1 (7h 55m). Back at 11:00 am or 12:35 pm. The same flights cost $1,795 if booked directly with British Airways.\n- **American Airlines, $1,786:** Nonstop, shown as a sponsored ad. I didn't see its flight times.\n\n**Cheapest overall: $1,216, with caveats**\n- It is a self-transfer itinerary, meaning separate tickets with no through-protection.\n- Outbound is Aer Lingus and Ryanair with 1 stop in Dublin (2h 50m layover). It leaves at 8:05 pm and arrives at 1:40 pm+1 at Stansted (STN), 11h 35m in total.\n- Return is Ryanair and Icelandair with 2 stops: Stockholm (13h 25m layover), then Reykjavik (1h 15m layover). It leaves at 8:00 pm and arrives at 5:20 pm+1, 27h 20m in total.\n\nThe cheapest nonstop is $1,767 with Iberia. I haven't booked anything. To book one, use the \"Select\" button on Kayak, or I can narrow the results further.",
